      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T15:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we more timing-attack resistant by writing `std::min(255.0f / a, FLT_MAX)`? The comparison-and-ternary may introduce a timing variation.\n\nThis seems like it would guard against nan from `c * invA` below, because `0 * FLT_MAX` is still zero (unlike `0 * inf` if we left off the `min` entirely).\n```suggestion\n    const float invA \u003d std::min(255.0f / a, FLT_MAX);\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "04f9ba6904679e175e89c135d5fb360905d4b3df",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a257e769_624cdf91",
        "filename": "src/opts/SkSwizzler_opts.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T15:11:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, it\u0027ll make everything with a\u003d0 turn transparent white instead of transparent black. Not sure if that is a problem.",
      "parentUuid": "a28dabdb_44704ba1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "04f9ba6904679e175e89c135d5fb360905d4b3df",
